        {
          "path": "_m/u/5/j/n/atlantic-ocean-road-wp/atlantic-ocean-road-norway-ast.jpg",
          "filename": "Atlantic Ocean Road, Norway (ASTER).jpg",
          "caption": "The Atlantic Ocean Road is an 8.3 kilometer road that runs through an archipelago in Eide and Averoy in More of Romsdal, Norway. It consists of eight bridges and four resting places and viewpoints. The road was originally proposed as a railway line, but that was abandoned. The road was opened in July 1989, and has been declared the world’s best road trip. The image was acquired July 2, 2008, covers an area of 8.9 by 11.8 kilometers, and is located at 63 degrees north, 7.3 degrees east.",
          "alt": "The Atlantic Ocean Road is an 8.3 kilometer road that runs through an archipelago in Eide and Averoy in More of Romsdal, Norway. It consists of eight bridges and four resting places and viewpoints. The road was originally proposed as a railway line, but that was abandoned. The road was opened in July 1989, and has been declared the world’s best road trip. The image was acquired July 2, 2008, covers an area of 8.9 by 11.8 kilometers, and is located at 63 degrees north, 7.3 degrees east.",
          "width": 789,
          "height": 590,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "Public domain",
          "artist": "NASA/METI/AIST/Japan Space Systems, and U.S./Japan ASTER Science Team",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlantic_Ocean_Road,_Norway_(ASTER).jpg",
